 "version": "1.7.3",
 "changelog": "Hold completion fix from your Windows test of v1.7.2 - the app could keep saying Holding after the button had already finished and been removed, and then never scanned again. What changed: (1) The hold watcher now releases as soon as the button is confirmed gone (two missed looks in a row). (2) A frozen fill counts as completed: if the fill does not grow at all for 6 seconds, the hold ends there instead of waiting for the 300 second safety limit - this was the real deadlock, a leftover of the finished button kept matching as a filling button with a frozen fill. (3) The log now prints a Watch line whenever the watched state changes and at least every 2 seconds during a hold (state, confidence, fill, miss count), so what the watcher sees is always visible. (4) Scan errors now show the real quick and full detect errors, a quick pass failure no longer cancels the full detect, and the mss deprecation warnings are gone from the log.",
